Author: Konrad <konrad@MacBook-Pro-von-Konrad.local>
Date:   Sat Oct 17 01:03:15 2026 +0800

    Keyboard: give games key codes instead of iPadOS text input
    
    Hollow Knight's Unity/SDL toplevel enables zwp_text_input_v3, so every printable key was
    routed into the iPad text system and reached the game as a commit_string, which a game
    ignores. Only Enter survived, because insertText turns it back into a Return key press
    for a field that is not multiline. That is the reported symptom on the Magic Keyboard:
    Enter works, no other key does.
    
    LinuxTextInputMode lists the Wayland app ids whose hardware keys go to the app as key
    codes; hollow_knight.x86_64 is the default list, "Always Send Keys" covers every app and
    "Always Compose Text" restores the previous behaviour. Settings -> Keyboard exposes the
    mode and the id list, so another game can be added without a rebuild. A composition in
    progress (dictation, emoji, a dead key) still goes through the text system.
    
    Verified: DesktopKit's unit tests pass (379, including 8 new ones) and the user reports
    that the keyboard in Hollow Knight works on build 4453 installed on the physical iPad.
    Only that report is recorded: no per-key list, no measurement, and no log-level proof of
    the arriving key codes (the ishwl key log is part of the pending wl-bridge change).

